  "title": "Erdős Problem #929",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 2$ be large and let $S(k)$ be the minimal $x$ such that there is a positive density set of $n$ where $ n+1,n+2,\\ldots,n+k $ are all divisible by primes $\\leq x$.\nEstimate $S(k)$ - in particular, is it true that $S(k)\\geq k^{1-o(1)}$?",
